          "court": "Court of Appeals of North Carolina",
          "year": 2005,
          "date_decided": "2005-11-15",
          "holding": "The Court of Appeals vacated the visitation portion of a dispositional order because the trial court improperly delegated visitation entirely to the discretion of the custodian instead of establishing an appropriate court-approved visitation plan.",
          "relevance": "A guardianship or custody award must still contain a court-established visitation plan for the parent.",
          "quote": "The trial court maintains the responsibility to ensure that an appropriate visitation plan is established within the dispositional order.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/7473384/in-re-ec/",
